INT. DEEP-SEA HABITAT "THRESHOLD" - MAIN CABIN - NIGHT CYCLE

A curved steel cylinder lined with cables, plastic crates, and pipe. Portholes the size of dinner plates show nothing but black water. A single red emergency lamp pulses at the far bulkhead.

NADIRA SHARIFOVA (40s, habitat commander, close-cropped hair, a mug that reads WORLD'S OKAYEST BOSS) stands at the central console. PETRUS VAN DER LINDE (50s, pressure technician, ginger beard gone grey at the chin) kneels beside an open floor panel, a wrench in each hand. QUILL (20s, oceanographer, real name Quillon Adeyemi, dreadlocks tied up in a net) bends over a bank of sonar monitors, headphones around his neck.

NADIRA
(to the room)
Eyes up, everyone. Status report.

PETRUS
Seal four is weeping.

QUILL
Sonar's reading something big.

NADIRA
How big?

QUILL
Bigger than us.

Nadira sets down her mug.

NADIRA
(to Quill)
Define "something."

QUILL
It's moving. Slowly. Circling.

PETRUS
(muttering, to himself)
Not today. Not today. Not today.

He tightens a bolt. A thin jet of water hisses at his wrist, and he curses and clamps a hand over it. Nadira drops beside him and slaps a patch over the leak.

NADIRA
Hold it.

PETRUS
I am holding it.

NADIRA
Hold it harder.

The emergency lamp pulses faster. Quill removes his headphones, puts them back on, and removes them again.

QUILL
It's gone.

NADIRA
Gone where?

QUILL
Just gone. Vanished off the screen.

The hull shudders. A deep, resonant note rolls through the walls, like a cello string the size of a whale. Everyone freezes. Dust drifts from the ceiling. Petrus lets go of the patch, and it holds.

PETRUS
(whispering)
That was no engine.

QUILL
(whispering)
That was a song.

NADIRA
(to everyone, quietly)
Nobody panic.

She looks at the nearest porthole. A vast, pale eye slides past the glass, unblinking, then drifts into the dark.

QUILL
(grinning, helpless)
That's a sperm whale.

PETRUS
It's enormous.

NADIRA
(to herself)
Of course it is.

She retrieves her mug and takes a long, slow sip. Her hand shakes only a little.
